{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Only flesh with its soul its blood</b> Rashi wrote: while its soul is still in it — \"flesh with its soul you shall not eat\" — this is a limb from a living animal; and \"its blood you shall not eat\" — this is blood from a living animal. If so, Scripture should have said: \"flesh with its soul and its blood you shall not eat.\" But according to the plain sense this is not correct, and according to the midrash it is not true, for the sons of Noah were commanded only concerning a limb from a living animal, according to the words of the Sages (Sanhedrin 59a), not concerning blood from a living animal, according to the words of Rabbi Ḥanina ben Gamliel (ibid.). Rather, its meaning is: \"only flesh — with its soul, which is its blood — you shall not eat,\" for \"the soul of all flesh is its blood.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:26:15.273410608Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}